<article class="env-lemma" id="0DKR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0DKR">Lemma <span data-tag="0DKR">76.52.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of algebraic spaces over $S$ which is flat and locally of finite presentation. The full subcategory of $D(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ consisting of $Y$-perfect objects is a saturated<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001473745" id="a0001473745-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> triangulated subcategory. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Cohomology on Sites, Lemmas <a href="/tag/08FV" data-tag="08FV">21.45.4</a>, <a href="/tag/08FW" data-tag="08FW">21.45.6</a>, <a href="/tag/08G2" data-tag="08G2">21.46.6</a>, and <a href="/tag/08G3" data-tag="08G3">21.46.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>